{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon","id":937797,"title":"wonderandawe's Random Sidereal Thoughts and Head Canon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-26T15:26:06-07:00","id":937797,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> wonderandawe's Random Sidereal Thoughts and Head Canon","content":"I'm a bit of a Sidereal fan girl and thus have a lot of random thoughts about Sidereals floating around my head. This is going to be the thread where I record all of this crazy head canon. It's not going to be organized any sort of matter. Just as things occur to me and I feel like writing them down.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to put the table of contents in this post. Future posts will contain actually content. Feel free to comment, rip apart, make fun of my poor grammar/spelling, whatever else people post on this forum.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=937798#post937798\">Passing of the Torch</a> - How a new Sidereal is chosen and trained<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=937804#post937804\">Astrological Coordinates</a> - The easy way to find someone on the Loom of Fate<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=939213#post939213\">Arcane Fate</a> - Who is immune and why<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=939216#post939216\">Resplendent Destinies</a> - Trappings and how a destiny is perceived by other Sidereals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 07-28-2016, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T15:28:06-07:00","id":937798,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Passing of the Torch</u></b><br /> <br /> Barring unforeseen circumstances, a Sidereal is always given advanced warning of their death. While Sidereals can live to see five millennia, they do not always. The Maidens sometimes must cut the thread of one of their chosen early for the good of Creation.<br /> <br /> Decades ahead of their death, a Sidereal will receive a Red Envelope mission with their expected time of death and the name of their successor. The Sidereal\u2019s successor is usually an infant no more than a few months old. While this infant does not yet carry a Sidereal Exaltation, they are breastfed by their patron Maiden. With the Maiden\u2019s milk comes insight that other children do not have.<br /> <br /> It varies what a Sidereal does with the knowledge of their coming end. Some take the responsibility of training their successor seriously. They visit their successor\u2019s family and become an integral part of the child\u2019s upbringing. The child may hear the creaking of the Alchemist\u2019s cart and run to see their beloved Uncle Wang. Other\u2019s kidnap the child and raise them in Yu-Shan as their own. A few unable to deal with their foreseen end, will ignore the mission and the child. Often, the child exalts without any knowledge of what is happening to them. If the future Sidereal is lucky, some other Sidereal will find out about the mission while sorting the dead Sidereal's belongings and go collect the hapless Sidereal. Often they are not found until they do something that changes the destiny of Creation.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, events happen that defy destiny. A Sidereal will die unexpectedly. The Maidens do not chose whom to exalt lightly. It could take decades before they decide and then the Five Score Fellowship must wait for the future Sidereal to grow up. In such cases, an Elder Sidereal is assigned to watch over the child.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> I got this idea from the movie the Kingsman and from myths where goddess breastfeed mortal children they grow fond of.<br /> <br /> Also the trope of the mentor dying during a hero's journey it too good to pass up.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 07-27-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T15:43:53-07:00","id":937804,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Astrological Coordinates</u></b><br /> <br /> In Database Design theory, there is a concept called \u201cPrimary Key\u201d - each record in a table has an identifier (field or a combination of fields) unique to only that record. The easiest way to find this record would be to use this primary key. For the Loom of Fate, there is also a \u201cPrimary Key\u201d, an easy way for Pattern Spiders to find a thread in Loom. Pulling from Western Astrology, we can use a person\u2019s name, the location where they first entered the Loom (Usually the place of birth), and the time they first entered the Loom (time of birth for most individuals). With these Astrological coordinates, a Sidereal can easily locate someone on the Loom of Fate.<br /> <br /> For example, Hisakawa Mayu was born in Blooming Blossoms Hospital, Lookshy, River Provinces during the fifth day of Season of Descending Water, 6457 years since the fall of the Primordials at 3:32 in the afternoon. Even in a city as large as Lookshy, the odds are no one else named Hisakawa Mayu would be born at that hospital at that same time. If there is such a duplication, the second Hisasakwa Mayu may find themselves going by the nickname \u201cYuki\u201d or something like that.<br /> <br /> Now Mayu has never been to the Wyld, so her key on the Loom would still be her birth name and the location and time of her birth. When one stays in the Wyld long enough, their thread ends. When they reenter Creation, they get a new thread of Fate. A Lunar by the name of Phelps Navi has managed to outrun the Wyld Hunt and made it to the edge of Creation. His current thread on the Loom ends. After a few months, he returns to Creation. The Silver Pact has given him a new name \u2013 Leaping Salmon. Once he starts interacting with the Creation again, he is given a new thread with a new key - Leaping Salmon, Twenty- First Day of Resplendent Fire, 6487 years since the fall of the Primordials, Burning Tumbleweed Village, Unclaimed land in the Direction of Fire.<br /> <br /> If Mayu exalts as a Solar, it would be easy for a Sidereal to go to Lookshy and pull Mayu\u2019s birth records. If they were accurate, a Sidereal would easily be able to find Mayu on the Loom of Fate. If the Sidereal that does this is a Bronze Faction, Mayu may have a hard time outrunning the Wyld Hunt. If the Sidereal is Gold Faction, Mayu\u2019s birth records are mysteriously lost.<br /> <br /> In the First Age, the Sidereals and Gods in the Bureau of Destiny had a directory with a list of names, birthdates, and birth locations for important Exalts. Imagine the grumbling when Dashing Waves, a Solar Eclipse, goes yet again on another Diplomatic mission to the Fair Folk and the directory has to be updated\u2026again. Of course, during the Usurpation, this directory was quite handy for tracking down fleeing Solars.<br /> <br /> Of course, not all of Creation keep detailed records of birth like the Scarlet Empire and Lookshy, but that is another post.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I work with databases every day, so this post may be an example of letting your real life job influence too much with your gaming.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 07-26-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:01:28-07:00","id":938051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=937804#post937804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Astrological Coordinates</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're saying... if a Sidereal wants to keep track on every Terrestrial Exalted in Creation...<br /> They'd have a great DB DB?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I absolutely love the idea of making the Loom of Fate a form of database (fits Autochthon's style, alright). One can even argue that's it's a very unorganized Graph Database, what with the N:N configuration, and the procedural queries (why else would the Investigation roll take <b>so damn long</b>?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:07:57-07:00","id":938054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=938051#post938051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you're saying... if a Sidereal wants to keep track on every Terrestrial Exalted in Creation...<br /> They'd have a great DB DB?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Yeah, I guess so. I got the idea of the First Age Astrological Coordinate Directory from the government Blue Blue which has the contact information for all of the Senators and Representatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=938051#post938051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I absolutely love the idea of making the Loom of Fate a form of database (fits Autochthon's style, alright). One can even argue that's it's a very unorganized Graph Database, what with the N:N configuration, and the procedural queries (why else would the Investigation roll take <b>so damn long</b>?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was reading though the Loom of Fate section and realized that Sidereals are basically Data Miners. I went to grad school for Data Mining! Which is going to be my next post - Finding people who you don't have Astrological coordinates for. Just need to get the Hero draft finished before I clean the next Loom Post up.<br /> <br /> I got a few ideas of threads of Fate being joined (or connected) via the thread owner's intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:19:45-07:00","id":938058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=938054#post938054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a few ideas of threads of Fate being joined (or connected) via the thread owner's intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof, that's an almost-complete Graph right there.<br /> What joins location threads, by the way? &quot;People who visited/lived in &lt;Place&gt; during &lt;Date&gt;?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T06:24:49-07:00","id":938059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=938058#post938058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oof, that's an almost-complete Graph right there.<br /> What joins location threads, by the way? &quot;People who visited/lived in &lt;Place&gt; during &lt;Date&gt;?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Locations are groups of people. If a person is a cobweb like thread, then a location is multiple threads wrapped together in a strand. (I'm also a knitter, so I'm pulling these ideas from all my hobbies) Groups of people have beliefs and intimacies that may connect to other locations and individual connections like relatives and friends and such. It's why the Order Conferring Trade pattern was so important to the stability of Creation. It got people moving around and making connections with new people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:28:05-07:00","id":938098,"title":"","content":"We have the idea of the Order Conferring Trade Pattern weaving people through Creation and making them less susceptible to Wyld influence. We also have the idea of folks heading out to the Wyld and their thread 'ending' or being lost after so much non-contact with the rest of the tapestry.<br /> <br /> But what I'm wondering is why multiple threads would be more resistant, and why that multiple thread resistance wouldn't be just as strong if, say, a bunch of people took a Wyld exodus? I'd love to hear some Sidereal/Loom/Fate headcannon on that. <br /> <br /> Like, is it a degree of freedom thing? If only one thread is looking at one rock from one side then the Wyld can change the other unobserved side? Like in the bordermarches how most things seem real and normal until you turn around and suddenly the way you came isn't there anymore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:45:19-07:00","id":938107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=938098#post938098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have the idea of the Order Conferring Trade Pattern weaving people through Creation and making them less susceptible to Wyld influence. We also have the idea of folks heading out to the Wyld and their thread 'ending' or being lost after so much non-contact with the rest of the tapestry.<br /> <br /> But what I'm wondering is why multiple threads would be more resistant, and why that multiple thread resistance wouldn't be just as strong if, say, a bunch of people took a Wyld exodus? I'd love to hear some Sidereal/Loom/Fate headcannon on that.<br /> <br /> Like, is it a degree of freedom thing? If only one thread is looking at one rock from one side then the Wyld can change the other unobserved side? Like in the bordermarches how most things seem real and normal until you turn around and suddenly the way you came isn't there anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good questions!<br /> <br /> If you consider the Loom of Fate as a building a large extra dimensional tapestry, then more threads with a tighter ply means a stronger fabric. Groups at the edge of the Loom are more susceptible to Wyld Mutation and being lost if they don't keep strong connections with the rest of Creation. Also, as the group builds connections to creation, the area around them stabilizes and pushes back the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Solar charms do this at a more rapid rate. Similar to how mortals can do things to encourage Shadowlands to retreat, but there is a Solar level spell that can close the Shadowland up. Shadowlands and Wyld Zones are similar to rends in the fabric of the Loom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T16:39:45-07:00","id":939213,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Arcane Fate Thoughts</b></u><br /> <br /> Immunity from Arcane Fate for those inside Fate is defined by their access to the Loom. Gods of the Bureau of Destiny, Celestial Lions, and Auditors all have access to the Loom of Fate to complete their duties. Gods, Exalts, and mortals without Loom Access are affected by Arcane Fate. Star touched (Sidereal Half Caste) are not immune from Arcane Fate unless they work for the Bureau of Destiny and have gained access to the Loom. It is very rare for a mortal to gain access<br /> <br /> Acquaintances who retained enough memories of a Sidereal to develop an intimacy for them are basically immune from Arcane fate, but the relationship will always be plagued by forgotten birthdays, promises, and other details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T16:47:24-07:00","id":939216,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Resplendent Destinies and other Sidereals</u></b><br /> <br /> A Sidereal\u2019s Resplendent Destiny is often tied to a particular trapping. The list of trapping for each college is only a list of examples. An imaginative Sidereal can come up with a variety of appropriate trappings for their false identities. For example, Akachi, a Chosen of Serenity always wears a particular multicolored cloak when he dons his Peacock resplendent destiny. <br /> <br /> Other Sidereals can see though a Resplendent Destiny and know if you are in one or not. A Sidereal can roll Occult or Craft (Fate) to recognize which constellation a Sidereal\u2019s Resplendent Destiny is under, even if the Destiny\u2019s trapping is not visible. Members of a Sidereal\u2019s Circle can learn to recognize their circle mate\u2019s resplendent destinies without roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T17:17:32-07:00","id":939223,"title":"","content":"I'm rather hoping that if resplendent destinies are still more or less the same thing, they'll go back to explicitly being something that doesn't actually alter your appearance.<br /> <br /> (In First Edition, Arcane Fate made it trivially easy for Sidereals to disguise themselves even with highly limited means, and to fairly implausible purposes. This synergized effectively with resplendent destinies; not only do I believe that there was a certain bonus to conducting a disguise that adhered to the stereotypes of your constellation, there was also a soft incentive for Sidereals to make their destinies look different from each other and the Sidereal's true appearance, since somebody noticing that these people who otherwise feel extremely distinct were identical in appearance caused Paradox.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T17:26:24-07:00","id":939227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=939223#post939223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather hoping that if resplendent destinies are still more or less the same thing, they'll go back to explicitly being something that doesn't actually alter your appearance.<br /> <br /> (In First Edition, Arcane Fate made it trivially easy for Sidereals to disguise themselves even with highly limited means, and to fairly implausible purposes. This synergized effectively with resplendent destinies; not only do I believe that there was a certain bonus to conducting a disguise that adhered to the stereotypes of your constellation, there was also a soft incentive for Sidereals to make their destinies look different from each other and the Sidereal's true appearance, since somebody noticing that these people who otherwise feel extremely distinct were identical in appearance caused Paradox.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always considered Resplendent Destinies similar to Clark Kent and Superman. They look the same except for the glasses (which could be considered a trapping), but no one recognizes them.<br /> <br /> I have this Sidereal Character concept of a Chosen of Secrets that is a humble bookstore clerk by day and the Green Ghost, defender of justice, at night.<br /> <br /> I like to use trappings in my quest as symbolism to signify what destiny a Sidereal character is wearing. I'd probably do the same thing if I ever run a Sidereal game. &quot;Bob is wearing his arrow head necklace.&quot; &quot;Ah, he has donned in his Quiver destiny.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 07-28-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:51:22-07:00","id":940486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=937804#post937804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Astrological Coordinates</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't this make it trivially easy for the Bronze faction to kill every single Lunar and Solar the week after they Exalt? That would make playing one awfully hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:34:29-07:00","id":940568,"title":"","content":"Some cool stuff here that I think I might steal. Especially like the knowledge of one's death and heir. I would have thought the envelope more likely to be violet th a red though as it is concerned with endings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:18:44-07:00","id":940740,"title":"","content":"I still like the exaltation needing to be incorporated at first breath. The advanced warning of when they'll die is interesting. What if they're killed by something outside of Fate ahead of 'schedule'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:46:04-07:00","id":940763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=940486#post940486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't this make it trivially easy for the Bronze faction to kill every single Lunar and Solar the week after they Exalt? That would make playing one awfully hard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't think so for a few reasons:<br /> <br /> A. They would have to know that a particular person Exalts. Not all Exaltations are public<br /> B. Only in the Realm and a few other locations do they have good birth records. I remember reading in the books that Solars on the Blessed Isle have a bad time of it, but that may be different in Ex3. You have to be exact down to the minute to work.<br /> C. The Gold Faction usually cover the new Solars (and maybe Lunars) tracks first. Lytek would warn them about a new Solar and the Gold Faction would take care of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:47:57-07:00","id":940765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=940740#post940740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still like the exaltation needing to be incorporated at first breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea still too. This thread is mostly just me throwing out different ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=940740#post940740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advanced warning of when they'll die is interesting. What if they're killed by something outside of Fate ahead of 'schedule'?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I misread your question. The future Sidereal exalts early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 07-31-2016, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:58:11-07:00","id":940772,"title":"","content":"I have two Sidereal ideas:<br /> <br /> 1. No Sidereal is ever born or exalted on Calibration.<br /> <br /> 2. Even on the rare occasion that two Sidereals are born in the same year, they are never born on the same day. It's impossible for two Sidereals to be born under the exact same stars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 07-31-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T15:21:21-07:00","id":940875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=940772#post940772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. No Sidereal is ever born or exalted on Calibration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was <i>this</i> close to having the Hero Quest character be born during Calibration. Decided on the Season of Air instead. Svante has enough special snowflake stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/937797-wonderandawe-s-random-sidereal-thoughts-and-head-canon?p=940772#post940772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Even on the rare occasion that two Sidereals are born in the same year, they are never born on the same day. It's impossible for two Sidereals to be born under the exact same stars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooo... I like this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}